From: renaud <rlpirou@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:44:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] BTC-CORE hooks: spread latency updates

performance.network.spread-latency-updates, off by default. With the key
off PlayerList#tick is Paper's, behind one boolean test.

Vanilla sends every player the latency of every player it can see once
per 601 ticks, all in one tick: players times players entries at once.
With the key on, the counter of vanilla is a slot of that period and a
player is served in the slot of its place in the list: the same packet,
as often, one player per tick up to 601 players. The counter stays
within the period either way, so the key may change while the server
runs. A player whose place moves within a period may be served twice or
wait one period more.

From Gale "Spread out sending all player info" (Martijn Muijsers,
GPL-3.0-only), based on Purpur "Spread out and optimise player list
ticks" (James Lyne, MIT), as carried by Leaf. Gale keeps buckets of
players; the place in the list does the same with nothing to keep
(dev.btc.core.performance.LatencySpread).

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/players/PlayerList.java b/net/minecraft/server/players/PlayerList.java
index 9f80ad24b1288b4da35c7ac491989f1dbcbf3c50..3188f8b63c75375aaaa23c14028c870fcb3ed884 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/players/PlayerList.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/players/PlayerList.java
@@ -760,6 +760,16 @@ public abstract class PlayerList {
     }
 
     public void tick() {
+        // BTCCore start - performance.network.spread-latency-updates: each player gets the latencies as often as before, in the tick of its place in the list instead of all of them in one tick
+        if (dev.btc.core.config.BTCCoreConfig.networkSpreadLatencyUpdates) {
+            this.sendAllPlayerInfoIn = dev.btc.core.performance.LatencySpread.nextSlot(this.sendAllPlayerInfoIn);
+            dev.btc.core.performance.LatencySpread.forEachDue(this.sendAllPlayerInfoIn, this.players.size(), place -> {
+                final ServerPlayer target = this.players.get(place);
+                target.connection.send(new ClientboundPlayerInfoUpdatePacket(EnumSet.of(ClientboundPlayerInfoUpdatePacket.Action.UPDATE_LATENCY), com.google.common.collect.Collections2.filter(this.players, t -> target.getBukkitEntity().canSee(t.getBukkitEntity()))));
+            });
+            return;
+        }
+        // BTCCore end - performance.network.spread-latency-updates
         if (++this.sendAllPlayerInfoIn > 600) {
             // CraftBukkit start
             for (int i = 0; i < this.players.size(); ++i) {
